# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project AIRI – environment variable reference
# Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and fill in the values you need.
# Variables prefixed with VITE_ are bundled into the browser build.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 3D Model customization ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# VITE_CUSTOM_VRM_MODEL_URL
#   URL of a custom VRM 1.0/0.x model file to register as a built-in preset.
#   Accepted formats:
#     • Remote HTTPS URL:  https://example.com/my-avatar.vrm
#     • Public-folder path (place the file in apps/stage-web/public/):
#         /models/my-avatar.vrm
#   When set the model appears as "Custom Model" (or the name below) at the
#   top of the model selector and becomes the default on first launch.
#
# VITE_CUSTOM_VRM_MODEL_NAME
#   Human-readable name shown in the model selector.
#   Defaults to "Custom Model" when not provided.
#
# VITE_CUSTOM_VRM_MODEL_PREVIEW_URL
#   URL of a PNG/JPEG thumbnail shown in the model selector.
#   Can be a remote URL or a public-folder path (e.g. /models/my-avatar-preview.png).
#   Leave empty to show a placeholder icon.
#
# VITE_DEFAULT_MODEL_ID
#   ID of the preset that should be selected by default on first launch.
#   Built-in IDs: preset-live2d-1  preset-live2d-2  preset-vrm-1  preset-vrm-2
#   When VITE_CUSTOM_VRM_MODEL_URL is set the custom preset is registered as:
#     preset-vrm-custom
#   (This setting only affects users who have never visited before; returning
#    users keep whatever model they last selected in the UI.)
#
# Example – swap to a custom VRM hosted on a public server:
#VITE_CUSTOM_VRM_MODEL_URL=https://example.com/my-avatar.vrm
#VITE_CUSTOM_VRM_MODEL_NAME=My Avatar
#VITE_CUSTOM_VRM_MODEL_PREVIEW_URL=https://example.com/my-avatar-preview.png
#VITE_DEFAULT_MODEL_ID=preset-vrm-custom
#
# Example – use a VRM file placed in apps/stage-web/public/models/:
#VITE_CUSTOM_VRM_MODEL_URL=/models/my-avatar.vrm
#VITE_CUSTOM_VRM_MODEL_NAME=My Avatar
#VITE_DEFAULT_MODEL_ID=preset-vrm-custom

# ── Analytics (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#VITE_POSTHOG_PROJECT_KEY_WEB=
#VITE_POSTHOG_PROJECT_KEY_DESKTOP=
#VITE_POSTHOG_PROJECT_KEY_POCKET=
#VITE_POSTHOG_PROJECT_KEY_DOCS=
